# Installed dependencies.
#
# These were tracked, and it was costing five minutes of every deploy. Render's
# log named the phase outright — "Checking out commit ... in branch main" — and
# 32,057 of the repository's 32,266 tracked files were node_modules, 99.4% of
# them. Checkout time scales with the number of files it has to write, not with
# the size of the change, which is why a 183-line commit deployed slower than a
# 553-line one.
#
# The build command is `npm install`, and package-lock.json is committed, so
# the dependencies are reproduced exactly from the lockfile instead.
node_modules/

# Environment files
.env
*.env
**/.env
**/*.env

# Dry-run output of scripts/map-cloudinary-urls-to-r2-keys.js
r2-key-mapping.csv

# Apply-step plans and generated revert scripts
r2-apply-*.csv
r2-revert-*.sql

# The WhatsApp monitor's frontend is a separate repository that is often cloned
# inside this folder. It has its own .git — it must not be tracked here.
WhatsAppSummarizer/
whatsappsummarizer/
